    </exercise>
 
    <exercise workspace="7in">
      <statement>
        <p>If your group finishes early, try one or more of these:</p>
        <p>
        <ul>
          <li>Keep going past 20. How far can your group get before a number stops you cold?</li>
          <li>Go back through your grid and find a second, completely different calculation for three of the numbers.</li>
          <li>Which numbers did your group only manage with a factorial, a decimal point, or a square root? Are those numbers actually impossible using just <m>+</m>, <m>-</m>, <m>\times</m>, <m>\div</m>, and parentheses, or did you simply not find it yet? Make an argument either way.</li>
        </ul>
        </p>
        <p>Use the space below for scratch work.</p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>


</worksheet>
